          %title
          %p Daniel Freed is a mathematician at Harvard University.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://people.math.harvard.edu/~dafr/"} website
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dan_Freed"} Wikipedia entry
          %p
            Freed’s work revolves around the mathematical ingredients and foundations of modern
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            and of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+anomaly+cancellation"} quantum anomaly cancellation
            (which he was maybe the first to write a clean mathematical account of). In the article
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Algebraic+Structures+and+Quantization"} Higher Algebraic Structures and Quantization
            (1992) he envisioned much of the use of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+algebra"} higher algebra
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            and specifically in the problem of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            in physics for the description of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+field"} higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fields"} gauge fields
            and their anomaly cancellation. Much of his work focuses on the nature of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Freed-Witten+anomaly"} Freed-Witten anomaly
            in the quantization of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            and the development of the relevant tools in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+K-theory"} differential K-theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/6d+%282%2C0%29-superconformal+QFT"} 6d (2,0)-superconformal QFT
          %h2#selected_writings Selected writings
          %p Dedicated entries:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quantum+Fields+and+Strings"} Quantum Fields and Strings
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Algebraic+Structures+and+Quantization"} Higher Algebraic Structures and Quantization
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization+and+generalized+differential+cohomology"} Dirac charge quantization and generalized differential cohomology
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Loop+Groups+and+Twisted+K-Theory"} Loop Groups and Twisted K-Theory
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/Mathematical+Foundations+of+Quantum+Field+and+Perturbative+String+Theory#ContributionDistlerFreedMoore"} Orientifold précis
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Topological+Quantum+Field+Theories+from+Compact+Lie+Groups"} Topological Quantum Field Theories from Compact Lie Groups
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4-3-2+8-7-6"} 4-3-2 8-7-6
          %p
            On
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+geometry"} spin geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+operators"} Dirac operators
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/index+theory"} index theory
          %ul
            %li#Freed87
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Freed"}> Dan Freed
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Geometry of Dirac operators
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ma.utexas.edu/users/dafr/DiracNotes.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/FreedGeometryOfDiracOperators.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+anomalies"} quantum anomalies
            via
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/index+theory"} index theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Michel+Bismut"}> Jean-Michel Bismut
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"} Daniel Freed
                %em The analysis of elliptic families. I. Metrics and connections on determinant bundles
                , Comm. Math. Phys. 106 (1986), no. 1, 159–176 (
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01210930"}> doi:10.1007/BF01210930
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104115586"} euclid:1104115586
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Michel+Bismut"}> Jean-Michel Bismut
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"} Daniel Freed
                %em The analysis of elliptic families. II. Dirac operators, eta invariants, and the holonomy theorem
                , Comm. Math. Phys. 107 (1986), no. 1, 103–163 (
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01206955"}> doi:10.1007/BF01206955
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104115934"} euclid:1104115934
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instantons"} instantons
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4-manifolds"} 4-manifolds
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karen+Uhlenbeck"} Karen Uhlenbeck
              = succeed "," do
                %em Instantons and Four-Manifolds
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4613-9703-8"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4613-9703-8
          %p
            On
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+quantum+field+theory"} topological quantum field theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Lectures on topological quantum field theory
              = succeed "," do
                %em Integrable Systems, Quantum Groups, and Quantum Field Theories
              %strong 409
              (1992) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-94-011-1980-1_5"}> doi:10.1007/978-94-011-1980-1_5
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ma.utexas.edu/users/dafr/OldTQFTLectures.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Freed-TQFTLectures.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+field+theory"} classical
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Classical Chern-Simons theory, Part I
              %strong 113
              (1995) 237-303 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1006/aima.1995.1039"}> doi:10.1006/aima.1995.1039
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9206021"} arXiv:hep-th/9206021
          %p
            On mathematical foundations of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superalgebra"} superalgebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
          %ul
            %li#DeligneFreed99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Deligne"}> Pierre Deligne
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"} Daniel Freed
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supersolutions
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quantum+Fields+and+Strings"}> Quantum Fields and Strings
                    , A course for mathematicians
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.ias.edu/qft"} web version
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9901094"} arXiv:hep-th/9901094
            %li#Freed99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Five+lectures+on+supersymmetry"} Five lectures on supersymmetry
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/FLS"} ISBN:978-0-8218-1953-1
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/517862"} spire:517862
          %p
            and with focus on
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signs+in+supergeometry"} signs in supergeometry
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Deligne"}> Pierre Deligne
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"} Daniel Freed
              = succeed "," do
                %em Sign manifesto
